; =============================================================================
; ADR-061 asset gateway: on-chain ABI of a CIP-113 vault, version 1
; =============================================================================
; Extends asset-gateway-onchain-v1.cddl, whose definitions (claim, exit_claim,
; inclusion_proof, absence_proof, sweep_asset, vault_continuation_v1,
; floor_top_up_v1, sweep_paid_v1, shard_datum_v1, insert, shard_redeemer) apply
; unchanged. Everything here is Plutus Data. Constr(i, fields) is written
; #6.(121+i)([...]) for i < 7.

hash32 = bytes .size 32
hash28 = bytes .size 28

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Custody (D1, D2)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A CIP-113 asset's vault is a smart wallet of the pinned CIP-113 deployment:
;   vault smart wallet = base(Script(PLB), Inline(Script(h)))
; Its custody is every UTxO at that address; PLB spends each of them with the
; pinned deployment's base_spend_redeemer below. Two scripts, both multi-purpose
; Plutus V3 withdraw validators with permanently registered credentials:
;   e = ProgrammableVaultExitDelegate(vault parameters, plb_hash, max_inline_datum_bytes)
;   h = ProgrammableVaultValidator(vault parameters, plb_hash, max_inline_datum_bytes, e)
; Their handlers: withdraw runs the actions; publish accepts only
; RegisterCredential (TxCert constructor 0); spend and every other purpose fail.

; The pinned CIP-113 base script's spend redeemer (not ours; listed for builders).
base_spend_redeemer = #6.121([params_idx: uint, wdrl_idx: uint])

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; h's redeemer: asset-gateway-onchain-v1's vault_redeemer, constructors 0 to 8
; (Follow, 9, is rejected). Constructors 5 to 8 are EXIT-only and delegated to e.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
custody_redeemer = vault_redeemer        ; minus #6.1282([]) Follow

; e's redeemer: h's own action, mirrored. h requires e's withdrawal with exactly
; this redeemer for constructors 5 to 8; e learns h from it and requires h's
; withdrawal (D2, I46).
delegated_action_v1 = #6.121([custody_hash: hash28, action: custody_redeemer])

; For a deposit-shaped swept input, SweepExit's withdrawal key is its origin-keyed
; deposit_id (raw 32 bytes, below) instead of the outpoint, and `assets` carries the
; native entries followed by one entry #6.121([h'', h'', committed_lovelace]); the
; claim's asset_value is the native entries and its vault_lovelace the committed
; lovelace, which must not exceed the input's lovelace. Output 0 pays the native
; assets exactly and at least the input's lovelace. Any other input is swept as in
; asset-gateway-onchain-v1, by outpoint.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ProgrammableDepositDatumV1 (D6)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
programmable_deposit_datum_v1 = #6.121([
  beneficiary: hash28,
  refund_address: bytes .size 57,        ; a key-owned smart wallet of the pinned deployment:
                                         ; header 0x10 | network, PLB hash, stake key hash
  refund_key_hash: hash28,
  origin: #6.121([origin_tx_id: hash32, origin_index: uint .size 8, output_index: uint .size 8])])
; Deposit-shaped (the one total predicate, on chain and in admission): an inline
; datum that decodes as exactly this, judged on the decoded Plutus Data, so any
; list encoding is accepted. Any other datum is not deposit-shaped; decoding never
; fails a script.

; deposit_id = blake2b-256("deposit-cip113\0" || CBOR [vault_id, [origin_tx_id, origin_index], output_index])
; (strict deterministic CBOR of asset-gateway-v1.cddl). The record deposit/<deposit_id>
; keeps the original outpoint as history.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Rules
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; V14 vault inputs: every input at exactly the vault smart wallet; at least one.
; V15 no output has h or e as its payment credential; only the continuation sits at
;     the full vault smart wallet. Other payment parts with Script(h) as stake are
;     not custody and are allowed.
; V16 a continuation's ids number at most floor((max_inline_datum_bytes - 6) / 34),
;     29 at 1,024 bytes (and at most 64).
; V17 no certificates and no mint; withdrawals are not restricted by the script.
; V5  a payout carrying the asset pays a key-owned smart wallet of the pinned
;     deployment; a lovelace-only payout may also pay a key-payment address. No datum
;     hash, no reference script.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Shard binding variant (D5)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ProgrammableShardValidator(shard_thread_policy_id, h): asset-gateway-onchain-v1's
; shard with one predicate replaced: Script(h) is among the withdrawals (the custody
; handler ran) instead of an input with h as its payment credential.
